{
  "dom_id": "step-q177697",
  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "The $6$th and $7$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $-37$ and $-43,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence.",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nSince the terms ${a}_{6}=-37$ and ${a}_{7}=-43$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{7}-{a}_{6} \\\\  & =-43-(-37) \\\\  & =-43+37 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{7}=-43,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{7}$ is $6$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{7} & ={a}_{1}+6d \\\\ -43 & ={a}_{1}+6(-6) \\\\ -43 & ={a}_{1}-36 \\\\ -43+36 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-7+(n-1)(-6) \\\\  & =-7-6n+6 \\\\  & =-6n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
